LEGEND["<div style='width:320px;text-align:left'><b style='font-size:15px'>LAYER LEGEND — DSIC 2</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>🟣 layer 0 — the flow (time)<br/>🔵 layer 1 — the core (signed; spinor form)<br/>🟢 layer 2 — the projection (moduli)<br/>🟠 layer 3 — physics (observables)<br/>🟪 Part II — the second tier (binding, P6; space AND time)<br/>🟦 Part III — structure growth (fσ₈)<br/>⬜ gray dashed — invariant checks<br/>🟥 red dashed — the core's boundary</span></div>"]

ACT["<div style='width:300px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:19px'>𝒮[φ] = ∫ ½ φ̇² dt</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the action of the free flow φ; varying it gives φ̈ = 0 — nothing accelerates the flow</span></div>"]
PHI["<div style='width:280px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:19px'>φ = ω·t</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the phase grows uniformly at rate ω — irreversible time itself, the model's only dynamics</span></div>"]

S["<div style='width:280px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:19px'>S = R·sin(φ/2)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the scale of space (signed); an odd function of φ, it passes through zero and changes sign</span></div>"]
O["<div style='width:280px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:19px'>O = R·cos(φ/2)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the scale of objectness (signed); shifted by ¼ turn relative to S</span></div>"]
NORM["<div style='width:300px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:19px'>S² + O² = R²</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the master law: the norm is constant (a circle); scale only flows between the poles</span></div>"]
W["<div style='width:300px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:17px'>W = S·O′ − O·S′ = −R²/2</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the constant Wronskian: one pole at zero — the other at its maximum (quadrature)</span></div>"]
PSI["<div style='width:320px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:18px'>ψ = O + i·S = R·e^{iφ/2}</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the spinor form of the core: the norm |ψ|² = R² and the quadrature hold identically, not as separate postulates; period 4π</span></div>"]
MOB["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:16px'>ψ(φ+2π) = −ψ(φ) ;  ψ(φ+4π) = +ψ(φ)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the two-sheet (Möbius / SU(2)-spinor) covering — FORCED by P2+P4 for any phase rate; the minus phase of objectness is the second sheet, not a hand-set rule</span></div>"]
SIG["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>O_full = R·cos(φ/2)·sign[sin(φ/2)]</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the inherited sign without manual σ: Re ψ on the sheet set by sign Im ψ; continuous at object inversions, sheet-flip at space inversions — unobservable from inside</span></div>"]

PROJ["<div style='width:300px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:17px'>π : (S, O) ↦ (|S|, |O|)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the modulus operation: the sign is cut off, the mirror sheet is unobservable in principle; the observed period is half the sign period</span></div>"]
P["<div style='width:290px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:18px'>P = |S| = R·√(1−μ²)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>observable space (≥0); light propagates along this pole</span></div>"]
Q["<div style='width:280px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:18px'>Q = |O| = R·μ</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>observable objectness (≥0); the observer, their ruler and clock are made of it</span></div>"]
MU["<div style='width:290px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:18px'>μ = |cos(φ/2)| = Q/R</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the observable phase ∈ [0,1] — the fraction of objectness; the master variable of all the physics. μ→1 — the Mush (a physical state on both sides of the zero of space); μ→0 — the bounce of objects</span></div>"]
PQ["<div style='width:280px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:18px'>P² + Q² = R²</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the same norm in the projection: the modulus preserves the circle (a layer check)</span></div>"]

LT["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>L(μ) ∝ μ ;  dτ = dt/μ ;  c = const</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the observer's scales: the ruler stretches with objectness, the clock inversely to it; c = const pins both. The clock factor is defined only below the detachment horizon (see Part II)</span></div>"]
B["<div style='width:300px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:19px'>b(μ) = √(1−μ²) / μ²</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the scale factor — the heart of the model; one function, no functional freedom; all observable physics is derived from it</span></div>"]
Z["<div style='width:300px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:17px'>1 + z = b(μ₀) / b(μ_e)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>redshift: three contributions (space stretch × source clock × object ruler), each entering exactly once</span></div>"]
H["<div style='width:290px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:17px'>|H_τ| = (2−μ²) / (1−μ²)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the expansion rate (units of k): at the Mush → ∞, at the bounce → 2</span></div>"]
Q3["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:16px'>q = (−μ⁴+6μ²−4)/(μ⁴−4μ²+4)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the deceleration parameter; changes sign at μ_cross = √(3−√5) = 0.874 (z_t = 0.769) — acceleration from geometry, no dark energy</span></div>"]
WEFF["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:16px'>w_eff = (2q−1)/3</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the Friedmann reading of the same geometry: one effective medium sliding from +1/3 (radiation-like, at the Mush) to −1 (Λ-like, de Sitter limit); nothing new is introduced</span></div>"]
CHI["<div style='width:340px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:14px'>χ = (c/k)·[√(1−μ₀²)/μ₀²]·[√(1−μ₀²) − √(1−μ_e²)]</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the comoving distance in closed form; the particle horizon is finite by itself; D_H = dχ/dz holds to 5.7·10⁻⁸ (machine check)</span></div>"]
DL["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>d_L = (1+z)·χ ;  DM = 5·log₁₀(d_L/10pc)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the luminosity distance and the distance modulus — this is what is compared with the supernovae</span></div>"]
OM["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>Om(z) = (E²−1)/((1+z)³−1)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>a diagnostic, E = H/H₀; flat in ΛCDM, U-shaped in DSIC (minimum near z≈2). On current data the test does NOT discriminate: the sign of Δχ² is set by the H₀ normalization</span></div>"]

FIT["<div style='width:350px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>CONFRONTATION WITH DATA (blocks [0]–[4])</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>Pantheon+SH0ES (1657 SNe, STAT+SYS): μ₀ = 0.7600 ± 0.0091, Δχ² = +0.05 vs ΛCDM at equal parameter counts — indistinguishable. Joint SN+BAO (DESI DR2, 12×12): Δχ² = −5.0, weakly for DSIC; BAO χ²/dof 1.04 vs 1.36. + chronometers, age, z_t — all at a single μ₀ ≈ 0.76</span></div>"]
PRED["<div style='width:340px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>FALSIFIABLE PREDICTIONS (block [5])</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>a trace of the CORE, forced by μ₀: D_H/r_d −2.5% at z=3 and −4.9% at z=3.5 (Lyα window, reachable by DESI DR3); E_DSIC/E_ΛCDM = 1.15 at z=5, 1.47 at z=10; the U-shaped Om(z)</span></div>"]
CMBN["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:14px'>THE CORE'S BOUNDARY: the relic radiation (CMB)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>at z*=1089.92: 10936 vs 13873 Mpc, a 21.2% shortfall — the limit of the CORE (Part I); a consequence of the finite particle horizon (it saturates by z≈10). The second tier (below) closes this shortfall</span></div>"]

P6["<div style='width:340px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>POSTULATE P6 — binding / detachment</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the one new entity of the second tier: until the monolith of objectness has parted (on average along the light path), light has no path. The first objects are patches of the monolith that NEVER UNCOUPLED — expected early islands, no contradiction with JWST galaxies at z≈10–14. Form fixed by principle: amplitude A≡1, a sharp threshold</span></div>"]
CORR["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>correction ∝ 1/P = 1/√(1−μ²)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the addition to the light path in the stuck-together phase; the integral = arcsin μ. Identically zero at μ ≤ μ_d — the late Universe is untouched (block [9])</span></div>"]
MUD["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:16px'>μ_d = 0.9806  (z_detach = 4.526)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the DETACHMENT HORIZON — a measured constant of the second tier; calibrated against ONE observation (the angle θ*, Planck 2018), zero degrees of freedom; a calibration, not a prediction</span></div>"]
DMC["<div style='width:340px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:13px'>D_M corr = D_M + (c/k)·[arcsin μ_cmb − arcsin μ_d]</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the corrected distance to the CMB = 13872.8 Mpc; 100·θ_model = 1.04110 (Planck: 1.04110) — exact closure; distance duality and achromaticity hold by construction</span></div>"]

CLK["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>the clock domain of dτ = dt/μ</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>the SAME threshold read in time: the relative clock is defined only below the detachment horizon; inside the connected monolith there is nothing to measure time against — the clock is normal, dτ = dt</span></div>"]
TIME["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>piecewise background time t(z)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>rate-matched at μ_d, continuous (Δ ≈ 6.5·10⁻⁴ Gyr); the late Universe untouched identically. t(7.5) = 1.27 Gyr vs 0.71 in ΛCDM (block [6])</span></div>"]
ISL["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>island time of the observer</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>each patch switches to the relative clock at ITS OWN detachment z_form (an input from observations, not a parameter); built-in self-regulation stabilizes the budget at ~0.5–0.8 Gyr. Age of an early-detached observer: t₀ = 13.5–13.6 Gyr — inside the stellar anchor 13.5 ± 0.5</span></div>"]
SMBH["<div style='width:340px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>ISLAND TEST on real SMBHs (block [6b])</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>Salpeter budget vs island proper time for 6 observed early black holes: 5/6 accommodated at z_form ≲ 8–11 (observed assembly epochs); UHZ1 needs a heavy seed — the same conclusion its discoverers draw. A systematic failure at any reasonable seed would falsify the island picture</span></div>"]

GROW["<div style='width:340px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:13px'>δ″ + (2 + dlnH/dlna)·δ′ − 1½·Ω_m(a)·δ = 0</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>linear perturbation growth on the DSIC background (GR limit); f = dlnδ/dlna. Status — a survival test, not a derivation from the core</span></div>"]
FS8["<div style='width:330px;text-align:center'><b style='font-size:15px'>fσ₈(z) = f·σ₈·δ(z)/δ(0)</b><br/><span style='font-size:12px'>checked against Gold-2017 (18 points, WiggleZ covariance): χ²/dof ≈ 0.73 vs 0.74 — no worse than ΛCDM. The data are degenerate in (Ω_m0, σ₈) → the invariant S₈ = 0.761 ± 0.013 (block [11])</span></div>"]

